<title>PORTUGAL: Two percent of Sonae moved Lisbon bourse.</title>
<headline>Two percent of Sonae moved Lisbon bourse.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Most of the 869,200 shares traded in retail to industry group Sonae Investimentos on Friday, equal to some two percent of the company's capital, were the unwinding of a single position, traders said.</p>
<p>The stock closed just 22 escudos down at 4,527 escudos ($29.26). &quot;It seems to me that this operation is tied to the sale of a position held by a non-resident,&quot; said one trader.</p>
<p>Traders could not say who the investor was but the shares were sold through Lisbon broker Midas Corretora.</p>
<p>($1=154.73 escudos)</p>
<p>--Paula Cordeiro, Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
